.Dd January 8, 2021
.Dt G0WM 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm g0wm
.Nd a personal Wayland desktop environment
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl v
.Op Fl d
.Op Fl c
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
is a Wayland compositor based on wlroots.
It is intended to fill the same space in the Wayland world that
.Nm dwm
does for X11.
.Pp
When given the
.Fl v
option,
.Nm
writes its name and version to standard error and exits unsuccessfully.
.Pp
When given the
.Fl d
option,
.Nm
enables full wlroots logging, including debug information.
.Pp
When given the
.Fl c
option,
.Nm
writes the default settings to
.Pa ~/.config/g0wm/settings.json
and exits.
An existing file is kept and checked instead: every setting this build has
must be in it, and anything else in it is reported.
The same check runs at startup.
.Pp
Users are encouraged to customize
.Nm
by editing
.Pa ~/.config/g0wm/settings.json ,
whose built-in values come from
.Pa include/config.h
in the sources.
The key and mouse bindings live there too, under
.Em keys
and
.Em buttons .
.Sh STATUS TEXT
Every line
.Nm
reads from standard input replaces the status text in the bar.
.Em ^c#RRGGBB^
and
.Em ^b#RRGGBB^
set the foreground and background of what follows,
.Em ^d^
restores the default colours and
.Em ^^
draws a caret.
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
These environment variables are used by
.Nm :
.Bl -tag -width XDG_RUNTIME_DIR
.It Ev XDG_RUNTIME_DIR
A directory where temporary user files, such as the Wayland socket,
are stored.
.It Ev XDG_CONFIG_DIR
A directory containing configuration of various programs and
libraries, including libxkbcommon.
.It Ev DISPLAY , WAYLAND_DISPLAY , WAYLAND_SOCKET
Tell how to connect to an underlying X11 or Wayland server.
.It Ev WLR_*
Various variables specific to wlroots.
.It Ev XKB_* , XLOCALEDIR , XCOMPOSEFILE
Various variables specific to libxkbcommon.
.It Ev XCURSOR_PATH
List of directories to search for XCursor themes in.
.It Ev HOME
A directory where there are always dear files there for you.
Waiting for you to clean them up.
.El
.Pp
These are set by
.Nm :
.Bl -tag -width WAYLAND_DISPLAY
.It Ev WAYLAND_DISPLAY
Tell how to connect to
.Nm .
.It Ev DISPLAY
If using
.Nm Xwayland ,
tell how to connect to the
.Nm Xwayland
server.
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width "~/.config/g0wm/settings.json"
.It Pa ~/.config/g0wm/settings.json
Every setting
.Nm
reads at startup.
Written by
.Fl c ,
and by
.Cm make install
when it is not there yet; the values it starts out with come from
.Pa include/config.h .
It holds only the sections this build was configured with, so a build without
the integrated background has no wallpaper or blur settings in it.
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr dwm 1 ,
.Xr xkeyboard-config 7
.Sh BUGS
All of them.
